1x0d|a|Wet, so as to spatter easily; wet, as with something slopped over; muddy; plashy; as, a sloppy place, walk, road.	e:nqw,131,3;24gy,33,3~24gy,33,3;nqw,131,3
1x0k|n|A broad, flat, wooden bar; a slat or sloat. ; A bolt or bar for fastening a door. ; A narrow depression, perforation, or aperture; esp., one for the reception of a piece fitting or sliding in it. ; The track of a deer; hence, a track of any kind.	a:8xb,36,2;24hv,31,3;1tcb,2,1~24hv,31,3;8xb,36,2;1tcb,2,1	n:b00,84,30;1atb,70,3;1uij,58,5;1zf0,45,6;28d5,32,3;8xb,26,1;24hv,25,2~b00,84,30;1zf0,45,6;1uij,58,5;1atb,70,3;28d5,32,3;24hv,25,2;8xb,26,1
